---
import SpotTheFake from '../components/SpotTheFake';
---
<section class="section" id="problem" aria-labelledby="problem-title">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="section__head problem__head">
      <h2 class="display-2" id="problem-title">Try connecting to the network</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Two networks, both called <span class="mono">Wipkingen Airport Free</span>. One is the airport's, one is controlled by an
        attacker. Which sign-in page is real?
      </p>
    </header>

    <SpotTheFake client:visible />

    <div class="facts problem__facts">
      <div class="fact fact--lead reveal">
        <p class="title-lg">A network name (SSID) is just a label anyone can set.</p>
        <p class="fact__text">
          Anyone can broadcast <span class="mono">Wipkingen Airport Free</span>. Nothing checks who is behind the name.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="fact reveal" style="--reveal-index: 1">
        <p class="title">Your phone auto-joins names it has seen before.</p>
        <p class="fact__text">Been to an airport with that network once? Your phone may connect again on its own.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="fact reveal" style="--reveal-index: 2">
        <p class="title">The sign-in page can ask for anything.</p>
        <p class="fact__text">Email, card details, passwords. It is whatever the network's owner wants it to be.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style is:global>
  .quiz { display: grid; gap: var(--space-8); }
  .quiz__pair { display: grid; gap: var(--space-5); }
  .quiz__result { display: grid; gap: var(--space-4); justify-items: start; min-height: var(--space-8); }
  .quiz__result .lead { max-width: var(--measure-prose); }
  .problem__facts { margin-top: var(--space-16); }
  @media (min-width: 48em) {
    .quiz__pair { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--space-8); }
  }
  @media (min-width: 64em) {
    .quiz__pair { max-width: 60rem; }
  }
</style>
